# Profiling new CPython minor

If the change adds or extends a `PY_VERSION_HEX` / `sys.version_info` guard for
profiling (stack, asyncio, memalloc, ddup, collectors):

1. Update `scripts/profiles/profiling_versions.json` (or run
   `python scripts/verify_profiler_compatibility.py --scaffold X.Y`).
2. Refresh or add a baseline in `scripts/profiles/compatibility_baselines.json`.
3. Drive the migration with skill `migrate-profiling-new-cpython`; do not invent
   a one-off checklist.
4. Keep SSI/OCI disabled until CPython final. Do not claim memory parity without
   an A/B.

Detail: `docs/contributing-profiling-new-cpython.rst`.
Catalog: `docs/cpython-diffs/py315_pr_catalog.md`.
